n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"33:I[55169,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"TOCProvider\"]\n34:I[769,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"Sidebar\"]\n35:I[47486,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"ClientWrapper\"]\n36:T1ca7,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"import { Disclaimer } from \"../components/Disclaimer.tsx\"\nimport { Steps } from 'nextra/components'\n\n# Swaps\n\nAnoma Pay can swap one shielded token for another in a single atomic transaction. The user's token A leaves the shielded pool, is traded on a public venue, and the proceeds re-enter the shielded pool as token B in one on-chain execution. If any step fails, the whole transaction reverts and the user keeps their original balance.\n\n```\nprivate resource (token A) → [unwrap → swap on venue → wrap] → private resource (token B)\n```\n\nSwaps are currently filled through [Bebop](https://bebop.xyz), an RFQ (request-for-quote) venue where professional market makers quote a firm price. The quote's minimum buy amount is exactly what the user receives. Additional on-chain routing sources are planned, which will extend swaps to a wider set of tokens and venues.\n\n## How a swap executes\n\nA swap transaction is composed of three balanced resource legs:\n\n| Leg | What happens |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Token A unwrap** | The sell amount is unwrapped from the user's shielded balance to the `GenericCallForwarder` contract. |\n| **Generic call** | The [`GenericCallForwarder`](/anoma-generic-calls) executes three pre-committed EVM calls: approve the venue, execute the swap, and approve [Permit2](https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2) for the buy amount. |\n| **Token B wrap** | The guaranteed buy amount is pulled from the forwarder via Permit2 and wrapped into a new private resource for the user. |\n\nAll three legs are proven and executed atomically. The forwarder holds funds only transiently, inside the transaction, meaning that it has no custody of user funds before or after. See [Generic Calls](/anoma-generic-calls) for how this mechanism works at the protocol level.\n\n\u003cDisclaimer\u003e\nThe venue leg of a swap is public. The forwarder's trade on the venue is visible on-chain, including tokens and amounts. What stays private is who swapped. The trade cannot be linked to a specific Anoma Pay user and both the source and destination balances remain shielded.\n\u003c/Disclaimer\u003e\n\n## The quote lifecycle\n\nBebop quotes are firm but short-lived. Because the swap's out-amount is signed into the action tree before proving starts, the quote must remain valid through the entire proving window. The backend enforces this twice:\n\n1. **At validation**: the quote must have enough lifetime left to cover proof generation (a configurable safety margin). Too-old quotes are rejected before any proving cost is incurred.\n2. **Before broadcast**: a quote that expired while proofs were being generated aborts the submission rather than reverting on-chain.\n\nBoth rejections surface the stable error code `SWAP_QUOTE_EXPIRED`. On this error, fetch a fresh quote, rebuild, and resubmit.\n\n## Building a swap\n\n\u003cSteps\u003e\n### Fetch a quote\n\nQuotes are fetched through the backend proxy. The taker and receiver of the quote is the chain's `GenericCallForwarder`, not the user's wallet:\n\n```ts\nimport { TransferBackendClient } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nconst backend = new TransferBackendClient(\"https://backend.anoma.money\");\n\nconst quote = await backend.swapQuote(chain.network, {\n  sellTokenAddress: tokenA.address,\n  buyTokenAddress: tokenB.address,\n  sellAmount: 10_000_000n,                                  // 10 USDC (6 decimals)\n  genericForwarderAddress: chain.genericCallForwarderAddress,\n});\n// quote.buyAmount      — expected amount of token B\n// quote.minBuyAmount   — guaranteed minimum (what the swap actually fills at)\n// quote.expiry         — Unix timestamp; the quote is executable until then\n// quote.approvalTarget — contract the sell token must be approved to\n// quote.tx             — { to, value, data }: the venue transaction to execute\n```\n\nBoth tokens must be supported, wrappable registry tokens on the same chain. Only ERC-20 ↔ ERC-20 pairs are supported, native ETH cannot be a swap leg. Tokens eligible for swapping are tagged with `swapProviders` in the network configuration.\n\nRefetch the quote whenever it expires as a stale quote will be rejected at submission.\n\n### Build the forwarder calls\n\n`buildSwapCalls` produces the three EVM calls the `GenericCallForwarder` will execute. They are committed into the signed action tree, so nothing about the execution can change after signing:\n\n```ts\nimport { buildSwapCalls } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nconst calls = buildSwapCalls({\n  tokenA: tokenA.address,\n  tokenB: tokenB.address,\n  sellAmount: 10_000_000n,\n  minBuyAmount: BigInt(quote.minBuyAmount),\n  txData: quote.tx.data,                  // opaque venue calldata\n  destinationAddress: quote.tx.to,        // venue settlement contract\n  txAmount: BigInt(quote.tx.value),\n  approvalTarget: quote.approvalTarget,\n});\n// calls[0] — tokenA.approve(approvalTarget, sellAmount)\n// calls[1] — the venue swap transaction\n// calls[2] — tokenB.approve(Permit2, minBuyAmount)\n```\n\n### Resolve the swap resources\n\n`SwapResolver` assembles all three legs into a `ResolvedParameters`, reusing the standard resource selection for the token A side:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  TransferBuilder,\n  SwapResolver,\n  PayloadBuilder,\n} from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nconst transferBuilder = await TransferBuilder.init(\n  chain.transferLogicVerifyingKey,\n  chain.trivialLogicVerifyingKey\n);\nconst resolver = new SwapResolver(transferBuilder, keyring, chain);\n\nconst resolved = resolver.resolve({\n  senderResources: resources,             // the user's token A resources\n  tokenA,\n  tokenB,\n  swapAmount: 10_000_000n,                // excludes the fee\n  minBuyAmount: BigInt(quote.minBuyAmount),\n  calls,\n  fee,                                    // Relayer fee, paid in token A\n});\n```\n\n### Sign and submit\n\n```ts\nconst parameters = new PayloadBuilder(resolved)\n  .withAuthorization(keyring.authorityKeyPair.privateKey)\n  .build();\n\nconst { transaction_hash: txId } = await backend.transfer(parameters);\n```\n\n\u003c/Steps\u003e\n\nAfter submission the transaction follows the same lifecycle as a transfer, see [Transaction lifecycle](/transfers#transaction-lifecycle). \n\n### Slippage settings\n\nBy default (\"auto\"), the committed minimum is the quote's own `minBuyAmount` (the market maker's firm price). A custom slippage tolerance recomputes the committed minimum as `buyAmount × (1 − slippage)` instead.\n\n\u003cDisclaimer\u003e\nWith a firm RFQ quote, setting a custom slippage below the quoted minimum only lowers your guaranteed amount, it cannot improve the fill. \"Auto\" is the right choice for RFQ swaps.\n\u003c/Disclaimer\u003e\n\n## Errors\n\n| Error | Meaning | Handling |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `SWAP_QUOTE_EXPIRED` | The quote's remaining lifetime cannot cover proving, or it expired before broadcast | Fetch a fresh quote and resubmit |\n| `InsufficientLiquidity` | The venue cannot fill the requested size for this pair | Change the amount or try later |\n| Insufficient resources | The user's token A balance cannot cover `swapAmount + fee` | Change the swap amount |\n\n## What's next\n\nRFQ is the first swap venue, chosen because firm, longer-lived quotes fit naturally with proving-time constraints. Support for on-chain routing sources (DEX aggregation) is in the works, the execution model described above already accommodates them, and the SDK surface is venue-agnostic. Quotes arrive in the same shape regardless of where they are filled."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"x:mx-auto x:flex x:max-w-(--nextra-content-width)\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L33\",null,{\"value\":[{\"value\":\"How a swap executes\",\"id\":\"how-a-swap-executes\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"The quote lifecycle\",\"id\":\"the-quote-lifecycle\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Building a swap\",\"id\":\"building-a-swap\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Fetch a quote\",\"id\":\"fetch-a-quote\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Build the forwarder calls\",\"id\":\"build-the-forwarder-calls\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Resolve the swap resources\",\"id\":\"resolve-the-swap-resources\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Sign and submit\",\"id\":\"sign-and-submit\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Slippage settings\",\"id\":\"slippage-settings\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Errors\",\"id\":\"errors\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"What’s next\",\"id\":\"whats-next\",\"depth\":2}],\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"metadata\":\"$2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children:props:children:2:props:pageMap:19:frontMatter\",\"bottomContent\":\"$undefined\",\"sourceCode\":\"$36\",\"children\":[\"$L37\",\"$L38\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"39:I[83987,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"ToggleWordWrapButton\"]\n3a:I[63894,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"HeadingAnchor\"]\n37:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"id\":\"nextra-skip-nav\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"38:[\"$\",\"main\",null,{\"data-pagefind-body\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-bold x:mt-2 x:text-4xl\",\"children\":[\"Swaps\",\"$undefined\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":\"Anoma Pay can swap one shielded token for another in a single atomic transaction. The user’s token A leaves the shielded pool, is traded on a public venue, and the proceeds re-enter the shielded pool as token B in one on-chain execution. If any step fails, the whole transaction reverts and the user keeps their original balance.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-pagefind-ignore\":\"all\",\"className\":\"nextra-code x:relative x:not-first:mt-[1.25em]\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"pre\",null,{\"className\":\"x:group x:focus-visible:nextra-focus x:overflow-x-auto x:subpixel-antialiased x:text-[.9em] x:bg-white x:dark:bg-black x:py-4 x:ring-1 x:ring-inset x:ring-gray-300 x:dark:ring-neutral-700 x:contrast-more:ring-gray-900 x:contrast-more:dark:ring-gray-50 x:contrast-more:contrast-150 x:rounded-md not-prose\",\"tabIndex\":\"0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"x:group-hover:opacity-100 x:group-focus:opacity-100 x:opacity-0 x:transition x:focus-within:opacity-100 x:flex x:gap-1 x:absolute x:right-4 x:top-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L39\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"currentColor\",\"height\":\"1em\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M4 19h6v-2H4v2zM20 5H4v2h16V5zm-3 6H4v2h13.25c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2s-.9 2-2 2H15v-2l-3 3l3 3v-2h2c2.21 0 4-1.79 4-4s-1.79-4-4-4z\"}]}]}],false]}],[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"private resource (token A) → [unwrap → swap on venue → wrap] → private resource (token B)\"}]}]}]]}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":[\"Swaps are currently filled through \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://bebop.xyz\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer\",\"className\":\"x:focus-visible:nextra-focus x:text-primary-600 x:underline x:hover:no-underline x:decoration-from-font x:[text-underline-position:from-font] !text-anoma\",\"children\":[\"Bebop\",[\" \",[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":1.7,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"height\":\"1em\",\"className\":\"x:inline x:align-baseline x:shrink-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M7 17L17 7\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M7 7h10v10\"}]]}]]]}],\", an RFQ (request-for-quote) venue where professional market makers quote a firm price. The quote’s minimum buy amount is exactly what the user receives. Additional on-chain routing sources are planned, which will extend swaps to a wider set of tokens and venues.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"how-a-swap-executes\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-10 x:border-b x:pb-1 x:text-3xl nextra-border\",\"children\":[\"How a swap executes\",[\"$\",\"$L3a\",null,{\"id\":\"how-a-swap-executes\"}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":\"A swap transaction is composed of three balanced resource legs:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"x:block x:overflow-x-auto nextra-scrollbar x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:p-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"children\":\"Leg\",\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border x:border-gray-300 x:px-4 x:py-2 x:font-semibold x:dark:border-gray-600\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"children\":\"What happens\",\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border x:border-gray-300 x:px-4 x:py-2 x:font-semibold x:dark:border-gray-600\"}]],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border-t x:border-gray-300 x:p-0 x:dark:border-gray-600 x:even:bg-gray-100 x:even:dark:bg-gray-600/20\"}]}],\"$L3b\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$L3c\",\"\\n\",\"$L3d\",\"\\n\",\"$L3e\",\"\\n\",\"$L3f\",\"\\n\",\"$L40\",\"\\n\",\"$L41\",\"\\n\",\"$L42\",\"\\n\",\"$L43\",\"\\n\",\"$L44\",\"\\n\",\"$L45\",\"\\n\",\"$L46\",\"\\n\",\"$L47\",\"\\n\",\"$L48\",\"\\n\",\"$L49\",\"\\n\",\"$L4a\",\"\\n\",\"$L4b\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3b:[\"$\",\"tbody\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Token A unwrap\"}],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border x:border-gray-300 x:px-4 x:py-2 x:dark:border-gray-600\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":[\"The sell amount is unwrapped from the user’s shielded balance to the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"GenericCallForwarder\"}],\" contract.\"],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border x:border-gray-300 x:px-4 x:py-2 x:dark:border-gray-600\"}]],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border-t x:border-gray-300 x:p-0 x:dark:border-gray-600 x:even:bg-gray-100 x:even:dark:bg-gray-600/20\"}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Generic call\"}],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border x:border-gray-300 x:px-4 x:py-2 x:dark:border-gray-600\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":[\"The \",[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"href\":\"/anoma-generic-calls\",\"prefetch\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"x:focus-visible:nextra-focus x:text-primary-600 x:underline x:hover:no-underline x:decoration-from-font x:[text-underline-position:from-font] !text-anoma\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"GenericCallForwarder\"}]}],\" executes three pre-committed EVM calls: approve the venue, execute the swap, and approve \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer\",\"className\":\"x:focus-visible:nextra-focus x:text-primary-600 x:underline x:hover:no-underline x:decoration-from-font x:[text-underline-position:from-font] !text-anoma\",\"children\":[\"Permit2\",[\" \",[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":1.7,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"height\":\"1em\",\"className\":\"x:inline x:align-baseline x:shrink-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M7 17L17 7\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M7 7h10v10\"}]]}]]]}],\" for the buy amount.\"],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border x:border-gray-300 x:px-4 x:py-2 x:dark:border-gray-600\"}]],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border-t x:border-gray-300 x:p-0 x:dark:border-gray-600 x:even:bg-gray-100 x:even:dark:bg-gray-600/20\"}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Token B wrap\"}],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border x:border-gray-300 x:px-4 x:py-2 x:dark:border-gray-600\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":\"The guaranteed buy amount is pulled from the forwarder via Permit2 and wrapped into a new private resource for the user.\",\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border x:border-gray-300 x:px-4 x:py-2 x:dark:border-gray-600\"}]],\"className\":\"x:m-0 x:border-t x:border-gray-300 x:p-0 x:dark:border-gray-600 x:even:bg-gray-100 x:even:dark:bg-gray-600/20\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":[\"All three legs are proven and executed atomically. The forwarder holds funds only transiently, inside the transaction, meaning that it has no custody of user funds before or after. See \",[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"href\":\"/anoma-generic-calls\",\"prefetch\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"x:focus-visible:nextra-focus x:text-primary-600 x:underline x:hover:no-underline x:decoration-from-font x:[text-underline-position:from-font] !text-anoma\",\"children\":\"Generic Calls\"}],\" for how this mechanism works at the protocol level.\"]}]\n3d:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"[\u0026_p]:not-first:mt-1.5 [\u0026_p]:leading-snug mt-8 px-6 py-4 x:bg-primary-100 text-sm leading-snug rounded-md italic dark:!bg-neutral-700\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":\"The venue leg of a swap is public. The forwarder’s trade on the venue is visible on-chain, including tokens and amounts. What stays private is who swapped. The trade cannot be linked to a specific Anoma Pay user and both the source and destination balances remain shielded.\"}]}]\n3e:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"the-quote-lifecycle\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-10 x:border-b x:pb-1 x:text-3xl nextra-border\",\"children\":[\"The quote lifecycle\",[\"$\",\"$L3a\",null,{\"id\":\"the-quote-lifecycle\"}]]}]\n3f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":\"Bebop quotes are firm but short-lived. Because the swap’s out-amount is signed into the action tree before proving starts, the quote must remain valid through the entire proving window. The backend enforces this twice:\"}]\n40:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"x:[:is(ol,ul)_\u0026]:my-[.75em] x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:list-decimal x:ms-6\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"my-[1em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 leading-[1.65em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"At validation\"}],\": the quote must have enough lifetime left to cover proof generation (a configurable safety margin). Too-old quotes are rejected before any proving cost is incurred.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"my-[1em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 leading-[1.65em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Before broadcast\"}],\": a quote that expired while proofs were being generated aborts the submission rather than reverting on-chain.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n41:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":[\"Both rejections surface the stable error code \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"SWAP_QUOTE_EXPIRED\"}],\". On this error, fetch a fresh quote, rebuild, and resubmit.\"]}]\n42:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"building-a-swap\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-10 x:border-b x:pb-1 x:text-3xl nextra-border\",\"children\":[\"Building a swap\",[\"$\",\"$L3a\",null,{\"id\":\"building-a-swap\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"43:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"nextra-steps x:ms-4 x:mb-12 x:border-s x:border-gray-200 x:ps-6 x:dark:border-neutral-800\",\"style\":{\"--counter-id\":\"_S_1_\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"fetch-a-quote\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl\",\"children\":[\"Fetch a quote\",[\"$\",\"$L3a\",null,{\"id\":\"fetch-a-quote\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":[\"Quotes are fetched through the backend proxy. The taker and receiver of the quote is the chain’s \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"GenericCallForwarder\"}],\", not the user’s wallet:\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-pagefind-ignore\":\"all\"